## Goal

`createGame` takes `deckMarks`, a per-seat list of `DeckMark { index, radiant, upgrades }`. At setup, before §2.1's shuffle, the card at `index` of that seat's deck list is dealt on its Radiant face when `radiant` is set (B1). It then takes `upgrades` Buffs, `tune_once(…, TuneDirection::Upgrade, …)`, drawn from the game's `Rng` (B2). The marks are threaded through `create_recorded_game`, `ReplayInput`/`fold`, `replay_open`, `summarize_game` and a Glitch reset, so a recorded game folds to the same hash. With no marks, nothing is stored or drawn and the state hashes as before (B3). A bad mark refuses `createGame` with a reason (B4). Ruling R2702000 gets its note, a pending §11 paragraph, a §2.1 edit and its tests; the generated TypeScript types are committed.

